SET content = '<p>BUTUAN CITY | August 27, 2026 - For North Eastern Mindanao State University, participation in this year's Caraga Regional Science, Technology and Innovation Week (RSTW) went beyond joining a regional celebration. It was an opportunity to stand with fellow universities, government, industry, innovators, and communities in shaping what the future of innovation in Caraga could look like.</p><p>A key moment of the day was the MOA signing for the Caraga Regional Innovation and Startup Ecosystem (Caraga RISE), formalizing NEMSU's commitment as an institutional partner in building a stronger environment for innovation and entrepreneurship in the region. The partnership creates more room for ideas developed in universities to move beyond research papers and laboratories and find their way into technologies, startups, enterprises, and practical solutions that respond to real community and industry needs.</p><p>This is where NEMSU sees its role becoming increasingly important. As the University works toward its vision of becoming "A Research University advancing technology and innovation for sustainable development," partnerships such as Caraga RISE help create pathways for faculty researchers, students, innovators, entrepreneurs, and industry partners to work together. Good research matters. But research that reaches people, solves problems, creates opportunities, and improves communities matters even more.</p><p>NEMSU also joined the launching of the FSUU Food Innovation Center, highlighting the growing importance of research, technology utilization, food innovation, and academe-industry collaboration. The day concluded with the Stakeholders' Night, which brought together institutions and partners whose collective work continues to strengthen Caraga's science, technology, and innovation ecosystem. These engagements reflect the broader direction of the 2026 RSTW theme, "Science, Technology and Digital Innovation: Driving Food Security, Sustainable Energy and National Resilience."</p><p>For NEMSU, August 27 was therefore more than a day on the RSTW calendar. It was another step toward a future where universities do not innovate in isolation, where partnerships turn knowledge into action, and where science and technology ultimately serve the people and communities they are meant to benefit.</p><p>Because the best ideas do not grow in isolation. They grow when institutions connect, researchers collaborate, innovators are given opportunities, and communities become part of the journey from knowledge to impact.</p>'
WHERE slug = 'nemsu-strengthens-its-place-in-caraga-s-growing-innovation-ecosystem';
